  "methodology": [
    "Each model uses two workers in parallel; take the slower worker estimate, then sum 2B/4B/9B in serial.",
    "Non-generation overhead is measured worker wall minus summed batch_seconds, including asset/model loading, calibration, source and weight checks.",
    "Same-Q04 scenario multiplies the four new-dose smoke mean seconds on each worker by its formal record count; six selected points and one question cannot represent the full distribution.",
    "Old-length scenario takes all selected old dose=1 token lengths x4 at the measured worker median long-output token rate; lower doses may change lengths.",
    "Long-output rate uses actual 120-to-128-token records. Neither 4B worker produced a 128-token test response, so use its three 125-token records. No fabricated full128 throughput.",
    "All128 median and p90 scenarios multiply every new record by 128 and measured long-output per-token rates; p90 is interpolated empirical quantile, not confidence interval or hard bound.",
    "Formal estimates exclude queueing, transfer, export, archive, reading and further retries. Calibration/asset/model cost is included. Preflight is already measured and is not part of remaining formal runtime."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Only 24 newly dosed smoke outputs, all Q04 at six fixed middle points.",
    "No formal collection or qualitative scientific inference performed.",
    "Measured long-output rates have small sample counts and include repeat controls; future contention or hardware/runtime changes invalidate these extrapolations."
  ]
